structured.summary:
I wrote feat.clarifications.md, loop 1 of DES-03. No question blocks coding, and all eight stories can start on the approved design. The 13 sections are:
- the readiness result and the precedence rule;
- six form-only differences between the TRD, the stories and the design, each with the version to follow;
- about 50 doubts answered per lane (cross-cutting, Data Engineering, Data Science, Backend, Frontend and the end-to-end Testing Agent), each citing its source or marked as an interim answer or agent judgement;
- 7 new assumptions;
- 6 new non-blocking questions with owners, plus the carried questions and their interim answers;
- a readiness table per story, separating the [Pending] criteria from items that gate release only (feed v3 in production, the order against PROV-ACME-2026-11, and TQ-8);
- the proposed loop for new doubts;
- a validation check.
The verifier found 8 problems in the draft, all now fixed. Shell commands were not allowed in this step, so nothing was executed, and statements about Python behaviour are marked as agent judgement.

